<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">cargo</ansi>

All unworn items belong to company cargo, including companions' carried items.
Buying, picking up and receiving items puts them there. Items keep their exact
identity, enchantments, uses, quest marks and sharpened edges. A partly used
item keeps its uses.

Cargo load is the weight of unequipped shared items and your pet's pouch.
Worn weapons and armor do not consume cargo capacity.

Capacity comes only from assigned packs on living, present members and eligible
horses. Each member has one Pack slot. Cloth knapsacks and traveller's packs
provide 10 kg, satchels 5 kg, and frame packs 15 kg. Spare packs weigh something
but add no capacity. Assigned pack tare does not consume usable capacity.
A pack horse carries 40 kg, or 100 kg with a pack saddle (help mount).
Fallen or away carriers contribute no pack capacity (help pack).

At full capacity you cannot obtain more weight. Selling, dropping and eating
free space. Returning worn gear to cargo adds cargo weight and must fit. Removing a pack
is allowed even if it leaves you overloaded; all items remain yours.
Walking is never blocked, even if you lose a member and become overloaded.
Past 75% of capacity, route duration rises 10% and walking fatigue 8%; past 90%,
25% and 15%; at full capacity, 50% and 30%.

In combat, shared cargo does not count against any member's personal burden.
Worn weapons and armor affect dodge; assigned packs are dropped before
combat and do not count against burden (help burden).
No items can be used or assigned during a fight.

  cargo
  Shows weight, capacity, modifiers and contents.
  company equipment
  Shows exact item references; company equip assigns worn gear.
  company inventory
  Shows assigned containers, horses, cargo and treasury.
  company meal
  Feeds the company from shared supplies.

cargo put/take are retained as guidance: there is no separate personal backpack
to move items into or out of. In Company > Inventory, select cargo items directly
for comparisons, assignments and use outside battle.

